    "result_text": "Done. The build is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nIn `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (the handler behind `POST /api/owners`), I added an audit line emitted after a successful create via a dedicated logger named `AUDIT`:\n\n1. **Imported** `org.slf4j.Logger` / `LoggerFactory`.\n2. **Added** a class-level logger: `private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\");`\n3. **Emitted** the audit line right after `saveOwner(owner)` (so the owner's generated `id` is available):\n   ```java\n   AUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n       owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n   ```\n\nThe line carries the three required fields \u2014 owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate` \u2014 and is placed after all validation/rejection logic, so it only fires on a *successful* create. The `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` test (which attaches a Logback appender to the `AUDIT` logger and asserts a single line contains all three values) passes, and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
